# A Luxel library scene (Gitea #785) — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# `fit tile`: one 7x7 sprite repeated across the layout and ADDED over a
# pattern. Two things worth knowing are in these four lines. The box is
# `0 0 0 0`: under `tile` a zero box is the whole layout (docs/spec/scenes.md
# §4), while under `fill`/`contain` it would draw the sprite once at its
# natural size. And the pattern runs at 60 % so the sparks have somewhere to
# add INTO — added over a saturated frame they are invisible.
# No `U` line on purpose: this is a texture, so a bigger panel gets MORE
# sparks at the same 1:1 size rather than bigger ones.
S - Spark Field
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 60 none fill 1
N Twirls
I @pat/2d-spiral-twirls
L sprite 0 0 0 0 add 100 none tile 1
N Sparks
I @spr/spark
